> The game picks a spellbook that you don't already know (if it can). 
> Since the spellbook is 'plain' and not 'blank', it's still unknown. The 
> way to prevent this from happening is to try reading a plain spellbook 
> to ID it as 'blank'. Otherwise it'll just happen again.

The game will try (your XP level) times to find a spellbook that you
don't know that's in a school that you can advance.  If it fails that,
it gives you a random spellbook of any type.

Blank spellbooks aren't in any school if I understand right, so if
you got one there's a chance that you've already gotten most of the
types in the 2 schools Valks can advance.  You *should* read it to
learn that it's blank not plain, but if you've already gotten a
bunch of books it might not change the chances.  If you've only gotten
a few books so far and you're just low level so the number of tries
to give you an unknown one in one of your schools doesn't try many
times, reading it will significantly change the number of further
ones you'll get.

Basically when you get a spellbook as a prayer gift, it's a great
idea to read it very soon.  They are blessed so there's no risk of
ill effects other than the time it takes so any "safe" room will do.
Once you've read it, you will then get other types until you've
gotten bunches of types.

